    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's complicated, but like... if you look at the actual data on manufacturing jobs and wage stagnation in the US during that period, it's pretty hard to argue it was a success for workers, right? it feels like the \"new high-skilled jobs\" thing is kind of a reach when so many people lost their livelihoods. wouldn't it be more accurate to say it was a failure for the working class?",
